1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,770
Drop an apple, and it falls.

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,630
Newton said the Earth pulls it
down.

3
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:05,775
But Einstein figured out
something much stranger.

4
00:00:06,292 --> 00:00:09,632
Mass bends space and time, like
a bowling ball on a trampoline.

5
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:11,257
Planets aren't really being
pulled.

6
00:00:11,537 --> 00:00:12,577
They're just following the
curve.

7
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,958
The Moon is falling toward Earth
right now.

8
00:00:15,198 --> 00:00:17,558
It's just moving sideways so
fast that it keeps missing.

9
00:00:17,917 --> 00:00:19,477
Astronauts float for the same
reason.

10
00:00:19,797 --> 00:00:21,317
They're falling too, all the
time.

11
00:00:21,667 --> 00:00:23,227
Gravity even slows down time.

12
00:00:23,487 --> 00:00:26,427
A clock on the ground ticks
slower than one far up in space.

13
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:28,393
GPS satellites feel it.

14
00:00:28,593 --> 00:00:30,963
Their clocks gain about
thirty-eight millionths of a
second

15
00:00:30,973 --> 00:00:31,740
every day.

16
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:34,860
If engineers didn't correct for
that, your map would drift about

17
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:35,930
ten kilometres a day.

18
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:39,057
Pack enough mass into a tiny
space, and the curve becomes a

19
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:39,867
bottomless pit.

20
00:00:39,958 --> 00:00:40,758
A black hole.

21
00:00:40,778 --> 00:00:42,418
Not even light can climb back
out.
